{
 "schema": "bi-suite-manifest-v1",
 "doc": [
  "One entry per example. tools/bi_suite.py runs the entries this machine can run; see handbook/4-operations/regression.md.",
  "name      the entry, and the 'example' field of its result",
  "gpus      GPUs it needs on one node (default nodes: 1). nodes: 2 means two nodes with that many GPUs each",
  "quick     command for quick mode; full: command for full mode. A list is run step by step, even after a failing step",
  "result    where the bi-results-v1 file lands (default {run}/<name>.json)",
  "timeout   seconds per mode, for the whole entry; waiting for the runner's lock is not counted",
  "own_lock  true when the command takes the machine's lock itself, one launch at a time ({pylocked}, or a two-node launcher)",
  "committed optional: the result file behind the case page, compared by --vs-committed; with 'adapter' when it is in the example's own format",
  "python    optional: this entry's own interpreter (~ expanded); the entry is skipped where it does not exist",
  "Placeholders: {python} interpreter (the entry's own when it names one), {opguard} the OpGuard checkout (--opguard-root; entries using it are skipped without one), {repo} repository root (commands run there), {out} this run's directory, {run} this entry's directory in it, {result}, {timeout}, {pylocked} suite/bin/python-locked, {launcher2} the two-node launcher, {peer} the second node.",
  "Commands go through str.format: write a literal brace as {{ or }}."
 ],
